# AP2 - Acceptance test, debounced firmware (variant B: edge -> verify level after T)
# Date:      2026-11-07
# Firmware:  falling-edge IRQ masks itself, alarm after DEBOUNCE_MS = 10 ms reads
#            the pin level; LOW -> press accepted, HIGH -> rejected (release bounce)
# Basis for T: measured release bounce ~0.42 ms (PulseView, 8 MHz)
#            -> window 0.5 ms < T < ~50 ms, T = 10 ms
# Setup:     button GPIO 15 -> GND, internal pull-up; LED GPIO 14 via 330 R
# Precondition: Pico reset before test
#
# TC1: 20 presses, short and long mixed
#   Expected: press == 20
#   Result:   press 20, raw edges 20  -> PASS
# TC2: hold button for 5 s, then release
#   Expected: press +1 exactly
#   Result:   press 21, raw edges 21  -> PASS
#
# Coverage note: raw edges == press -> no release bounce occurred in this run,
#   so the bounce filter was NOT exercised here. See ap2_scratch_test.log.
# Note: only the final serial lines were recorded; full output not captured.

